# Storybook file location (app)

Story files for feature/module presentationals live in a **`stories/` sibling folder**, not next to the `.vue` file.

```text
features/<feature>/
  presentationals/     # Foo.vue
  stories/             # Foo.stories.vue  ← here
  containers/
  composables/

modules/<domain>/
  presentationals/
  stories/             # same rule
  composables/
```

## Rules

- Prefer **`*.stories.vue`** (Vue CSF / `sb-addon-vue-csf`).
- One story file per presentational (or one composed prototype story), named after the component: `MessageComposer.stories.vue`.
- Import the presentational with a **relative path into `../presentationals/`** (and fixtures/helpers the same way).
- Do **not** place `*.stories.*` inside `presentationals/`, `containers/`, or `composables/`.
- Containers stay out of the default Storybook catalog.

```vue
<!-- ✅ features/conversation/stories/ChannelHeader.stories.vue -->
<script setup lang="ts">
import { defineMeta } from "sb-addon-vue-csf";
import ChannelHeader from "../presentationals/ChannelHeader.vue";
</script>
```

```text
❌ features/conversation/presentationals/ChannelHeader.stories.vue
```

Design-system primitives may keep colocated stories under `packages/design-system` (shadcn kit convention); this rule is for **`@denser/app`** features/modules.
